      },
      "fernsteuerung": {
        "title": "Boiler remote control",
        "description": "With the boiler remote control (registers 48001–48046) Home Assistant can take over the setpoints of **all existing heating circuits and DHW tanks**. Switched on, a device \"Remote control\" appears with the select \"Control\" (Boiler controller / Home Assistant), the binary sensor \"Remote control active\" and setpoint entities per heating circuit and DHW tank.\n\nIt only takes effect once \"Control\" is set to **Home Assistant**. Home Assistant then sends all setpoints every minute; without a write the controller falls back to its own regulation after two minutes. A switching change (enable, DHW setpoint 0/above 0) waits up to ten minutes. After a restart the control is always at the boiler. Values you did not set are sent neutral (heating curve without heating limit, desired DHW temperature). A DHW setpoint above the tank temperature starts a charge – the replacement for the cloud's \"extra charge\".\n\nSwitched off, the integration neither reads nor writes these registers.\n\nSaving reloads the integration. Switching off removes the remote-control entities including their history.",
        "data": {
          "fernsteuerung": "Enable boiler remote control"
        }
      }
    },
    "error": {
